# IntraCore: параметры HAL блока из базы STM32CubeMX (db/mcu/IP/*_Modes.xml).
# Порождено tools/hal_import — руками не править. Формат: src/Docs/Description/HalCatalogFormat.md
[Ip]
Name=flash
Version=v1.0.0_U5_Cube

[Parameters]
# имя|подпись|группа|единица|мин|макс|описание
advanced_settings|Activate|Advanced settings||||<font color="red"><b>By enabling this feature, you have access to risky settings that could be harmful for your device.</b></font>
OB_Read_Out_Protection_active|Activate|Read Out Protection||||By activating the feature <b>Advanced settings</b>, the RDP values 1 and 2 when TZEN=1 OR 2 when TZEN=0 will be available to be set.
RDPLevel|RDP|Read Out Protection||||<font color="red">Bits 7:0 </font> <b>RDP[7:0]:</b> Readout protection level. OB_RDP_LEVEL_0: Level 0 (readout protection not active). OB_RDP_LEVEL_0_5: Level 0.5 (readout protection not active, only non-secure debug access is possible), Only available when TrustZone is active (TZEN=1). OB_RDP_LEVEL_1: Level 1 (memories readout protection active). <font color="red"><b>OB_RDP_LEVEL_2:</b>Level 2 (chip readout protection active) </font> When the readout protection level 2 is set: - The protection level 1 is guaranteed. - All debug features are disabled: . if OEM2 key has not been provided, JTAG and SWD are definitively disabled. . if OEM2 key has been provided under a lower RDP protection, JTAG and SWD remain enabled under reset only to interface with DBGMCU_SR, DBGMCU_DBG_AUTH_HOST and DBGMCU_DBG_AUTH_DEVICE registers to obtain device identification and provide OEM2 key to request RDP regression. - The boot from SRAM (boot RAM mode) and the boot from system memory (bootloader mode) are no longer available. - Only boot from main Flash memory is possible; all operations are allowed on the Flash main memory. Read, erase and program accesses to the Flash memory and SRAMs from user code are allowed. - Option bytes cannot be programmed nor erased except the SWAP_BANK option bit. Thus, the level 2 cannot be removed: it is an irreversible operation unless an OEM2 key has been provisioned (refer to OEM2 RDP lock mechanism). Note: The debug feature is also disabled under reset.
OB_BOR_Level_active|Activate|BOR Level||||
OB_BOR_level|BOR Level|BOR Level||||<font color="red">Bits 10:8 </font> <b>BOR_LEV[2:0]:</b> BOR reset level. These bits contain the VDD supply level threshold that activates/releases the reset. 000: BOR level 0 (reset level threshold around 1.7 V). 001: BOR level 1 (reset level threshold around 2.0 V). 010: BOR level 2 (reset level threshold around 2.2 V). 011: BOR level 3 (reset level threshold around 2.5 V). 100: BOR level 4 (reset level threshold around 2.8 V).
USERConfig|USERConfig|||||
OB_User_Configuration_active|Activate|User Configuration||||
OB_TZEN|TZEN|User Configuration||||<font color="red">Bit 31</font> <b> TZEN:</b> Global TrustZone security enable. Unchecked: Global TrustZone security disabled. Checked: Global TrustZone security enabled.
OB_NRST_STOP_UI|NRST_STOP|User Configuration||||<font color="red">Bit 12 </font> <b>nRST_STOP:</b> Reset generation in Stop mode. Unchecked: Reset generated when entering the Stop mode. checked: No reset generated when entering the Stop mode.
OB_NRST_STOP|NRST_STOP|User Configuration||||
OB_NRST_STDBY_UI|NRST_STDBY|User Configuration||||<font color="red">Bit 13 </font> <b>nRST_STDBY:</b> Reset generation in Standby mode. Unchecked: Reset generated when entering the Standby mode. checked: No reset generate when entering the Standby mode.
OB_NRST_STDBY|NRST_STDBY|User Configuration||||
OB_NRST_SHDW_UI|NRST_SHDW|User Configuration||||<font color="red">Bit 14 </font> <b>nRST_SHDW:</b> Reset generation in Shutdown mode. Unchecked: Reset generated when entering the Shutdown mode. checked: No reset generated when entering the Shutdown mode.
OB_NRST_SHDW|NRST_SHDW|User Configuration||||
OB_SRAM134_RST_UI|SRAM1345_RST|User Configuration||||<font color="red">Bit 15 </font> <b>SRAM1345_RST:</b> SRAM1, SRAM3 and SRAM4 erase upon system reset. Unchecked: SRAM1, SRAM3 and SRAM4 erased when a system reset occurs. checked: SRAM1, SRAM3 and SRAM4 not erased when a system reset occurs.
OB_SRAM134_RST|SRAM1345_RST|User Configuration||||
OB_IWDG_SW_UI|IWDG_SW|User Configuration||||<font color="green">Bit 16 </font> <b>IWDG_SW: </b>Independent watchdog selection. Unchecked: Hardware independent watchdog selected. checked: Software independent watchdog selected.
OB_IWDGSW|IWDG_SW|User Configuration||||
OB_IWDG_STOP_UI|IWDG_STOP|User Configuration||||<font color="green">Bit 17 </font> <b>IWDG_STOP:</b> Independent watchdog counter freeze in Stop mode. Unchecked: Independent watchdog counter frozen in Stop mode. checked: Independent watchdog counter running in Stop mode.
OB_IWDG_STOP|IWDG_STOP|User Configuration||||
OB_IWDG_STDBY_UI|IWDG_STDBY|User Configuration||||<font color="green">Bit 18 </font> <b>IWDG_STDBY:</b> Independent watchdog counter freeze in Standby mode. Unchecked: Independent watchdog counter frozen in Standby mode. checked: Independent watchdog counter running in Standby mode.
OB_IWDG_STDBY|IWDG_STDBY|User Configuration||||
OB_WWDG_SW_UI|WWDG_SW|User Configuration||||<font color="green">Bit 19 </font> <b>WWDG_SW:</b> Window watchdog selection. Unchecked: Hardware window watchdog selected. checked: Software window watchdog selected.
OB_WWDGSW|WWDG_SW|User Configuration||||
OB_SWAP_BANK_UI|SWAP_BANK|User Configuration||||<font color="red">Bit 2Unchecked </font> <b>SWAP_BANK:</b> Swap banks. Unchecked: Bank 1 and bank 2 addresses not swapped. checked: Bank 1 and bank 2 addresses swapped.
OB_SWAP_BANK|SWAP_BANK|User Configuration||||
OB_DBANK_UI|DBANK|User Configuration||||<font color="red">Bit 21 </font> <b>DUALBANK:</b> Dual-bank on 256-Kbyte and 128-Kbyte Flash memory devices. Unchecked: Single bank Flash with contiguous address in bank 1. checked: Dual-bank Flash with contiguous addresses.
OB_DBANK|DBANK|User Configuration||||
OB_SRAM2_RST_UI|SRAM2_RST|User Configuration||||<font color="red">Bit 25</font> <b> SRAM2_RST:</b> SRAM2 erase when system reset. Unchecked: SRAM2 erased when a system reset occurs. checked: SRAM2 not erased when a system reset occurs.
OB_SRAM2_RST|SRAM2_RST|User Configuration||||
OB_nSWBOOT0_UI|nSWBOOT0|User Configuration||||<font color="red">Bit 26</font> <b> nSWBOOT0:</b> Software BOOT0. 0: BOOT0 taken from the option bit nBOOT0. 1: BOOT0 taken from PH3/BOOT0 pin.
OB_nSWBOOT0|nSWBOOT0|User Configuration||||
OB_nBOOT0_UI|nBOOT0|User Configuration||||<font color="red">Bit 27</font> <b> nBOOT0: </b>nBOOT0 option bit. 0: nBOOT0 = 0. 1: nBOOT0 = 1.
OB_nBOOT0|nBOOT0|User Configuration||||
OB_PA15_PUPEN_UI|PA15_PUPEN|User Configuration||||<font color="red">Bit 28</font> <b> PA15_PUPEN:</b> PA15 pull-up enable. 0: USB power delivery dead-battery enabled/TDI pull-up deactivated. 1: USB power delivery dead-battery disabled/TDI pull-up activated.
OB_PA15_PUPEN|PA15_PUPEN|User Configuration||||
OB_BKPRAM_ECC_UI|BKPRAM_ECC|User Configuration||||<font color="red">Bit 22 </font> <b>BKPRAM_ECC:</b> Backup RAM ECC detection and correction enable. 0: Backup RAM ECC check enabled. 1: Backup RAM ECC check disabled.
OB_BKPRAM_ECC|BKPRAM_ECC|User Configuration||||
OB_SRAM3_ECC_UI|SRAM3_ECC|User Configuration||||<font color="red">Bit 23</font> <b> SRAM3_ECC:</b> SRAM3 ECC detection and correction enable. 0: SRAM3 ECC check enabled. 1: SRAM3 ECC check disabled.
OB_SRAM3_ECC|SRAM3_ECC|User Configuration||||
OB_SRAM2_ECC_UI|SRAM2_ECC|User Configuration||||<font color="red">Bit 24</font> <b> SRAM2_ECC:</b> SRAM2 ECC detection and correction enable. 0: SRAM2 ECC check enabled. 1: SRAM2 ECC check disabled.
OB_SRAM2_ECC|SRAM2_ECC|User Configuration||||
OB_IO_VDD_HSLV_UI|IO_VDD_HSLV|User Configuration||||<font color="red">Bit 29</font> <b> IO_VDD_HSLV:</b> High-speed IO at low VDD voltage configuration bit. This bit can be set only with VDD below 2.5V. 0: High-speed IO at low VDD voltage feature disabled (VDD can exceed 2.5 V). 1: High-speed IO at low VDD voltage feature enabled (VDD remains below 2.5 V).
OB_IO_VDD_HSLV|IO_VDD_HSLV|User Configuration||||
OB_IO_VDDIO2_HSLV_UI|IO_VDDIO2_HSLV|User Configuration||||<font color="red">Bit 30</font> <b> IO_VDDIO2_HSLV:</b> High-speed IO at low VDDIO2 voltage configuration bit. This bit can be set only with VDDIO2 below 2.5V. 0: High-speed IO at low VDDIO2 voltage feature disabled (VDDIO2 can exceed 2.5 V). 1: High-speed IO at low VDDIO2 voltage feature enabled (VDDIO2 remains below 2.5 V).
OB_IO_VDDIO2_HSLV|IO_VDDIO2_HSLV|User Configuration||||
OB_Boot_Configuration_active_NS0|Activate NS BOOT ADDRESS 0|Boot Configuration||||
OB_NSBOOTADD0_Address|Address|Boot Configuration||0x00000000|0xFFFFFF00|Non-secure Boot base addess 0
OB_Boot_Configuration_active_NS1|Activate NS BOOT ADDRESS 1|Boot Configuration||||
OB_NSBOOTADD1_Address|Address|Boot Configuration||0x00000000|0xFFFFFF00|Non-secure Boot base addess 1
